---
import "./dunstkreis.css";
import "./bluesky.css";
---

<figure class="fig strip-figure" id="blue-sky">
    <div class="blue-sky-panel" data-export="blue-sky" data-export-timeless>
        <svg aria-label="A ray of sunlight entering the air towards an observer, reddening as the air scatters it, with dots where it does"></svg>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Sunlight on its way through the air to an observer at the chosen height, from the side. The dots are the air
        scattering it, blue where that light is still white, golden where it has crossed much air. The bars show what
        arrives directly against the light above the air (dashed), what was scattered out, and what the sky adds, drawn
        five times as tall. Not to scale: the planet half as wide, the air four times as thick and scattering three times
        as strongly.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./bluesky";
</script>
